    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong uptrend (e.g., >85 EUR) followed by high volatility; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 3-6% in the first week.",
    "True outcomes display extreme mean reversion after initial spikes, often falling below model projections by 10-15 EUR within 7 days despite positive sentiment signals.",
    "Sentiment history (values >0.20) correlates with model overconfidence; when sentiment is low or neutral while price volatility increases, the model fails to capture subsequent sharp corrections.",
    "Forecast horizon error pattern: Model assumes linear growth based on recent highs, but true outcomes show a 'spike-and-crash' structure where early gains are quickly reversed.",
    "Apply downward correction factor of 0.85-0.90 to model forecasts when the last 3 days of history show >10% price increase and sentiment remains neutral or slightly positive."
  ]
